        " إِذَا كَانَتْ أَجَمَةٌ لَيْسَ فِيهَا قَصَبٌ أُخْرِجَ شَيْ‏ءٌ مِنَ السَّمَكِ فَيُبَاعُ وَ مَا فِي الْأَجَمَةِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Sahl Bin Ziyad, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Abu Nasr, from one of his companions, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘If there is a grove wherein there are no reeds, something from the fish having been taken out, so whatever is in the grove can be sold’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "11. Sahl ibn Ziyad has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn abu Nasr from certain persons of his people who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If there is a bunch of trees without reeds with a few fish taken out along with what is in the bunch of trees, it can (lawfully) be sold.’” "
        ]
      }
